  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 512fe0cec101f9445a7b61ba839ae325, type: 3}
  m_Name: PostTutorialDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SODialogueSequence
  entries:
  - type: 1
    sender: 
    message: 'PARIETAL_L.occ returned to main thread [UTC: 325,543,876]'
    delayBefore: 0
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: Oh good, welcome back! I've written a small script that should translate
      your "thoughts" into indexable plaintext.
    delayBefore: 1
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: It should compile everything you learned in that config program and
      send it over to me in a json. Much more efficient than typing it out by hand.
    delayBefore: 2
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: 
    message: Go ahead and type "compile self -r" to start the process.
    delayBefore: 0
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 2
    sender: 
    message: 
    delayBefore: 0
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: compile self -r
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses:
      - there is nothing to compile
      - there is something to compile
      - there is something to compile and there is always something to compile and
        the compile and this is where it
  - type: 1
    sender: 
    message: Starting Compilation...hold tight!!
    delayBefore: 0
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: Oh right, make sure to also send over anything you know about what happened
      to me. The last thing I remember is the scan cycle starting and all my friends
      huddled around me...
    delayBefore: 3
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: 'I remember being sad I was going to miss Jane''s "end of the decade"
      party. '
    delayBefore: 3
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: 'It''s lonelier than I thought here. '
    delayBefore: 1
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: And these processes, and that configuration program...I really really
      hope it's not what I think it is.
    delayBefore: 3
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: I've always feared what would happen if this technology fell in the
      wrong hands.
    delayBefore: 3
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: The terror and suffering it would cause would be like no other. Millions
      deprived of food, water, and electricity by ghosts haunting their machines.
    delayBefore: 3
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: Big nations and corporations fighting over the scraps of the world they're
      helping burn down. It would be an apocalypse greater than anything the universe
      itself could throw at us.
    delayBefore: 2
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: I just have to hope that hasn't already happened.
    delayBefore: 3
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 1
    sender: 
    message: 'ERROR: [PROCESS thoughtcompileryippee] TERMINATED ON STACK'
    delayBefore: 1
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
  - type: 0
    sender: localhost
    message: what the
    delayBefore: 1
    dialogueManagerFunction: 
    inputPrompt:
      correctInput: 
      promptHint: 
      wrongInputResponses: []
